@obverse
1. a-na a-šur-ne₂-me-di₂
#tr.en.(o 2): Speak to Aššur-nēmedī, thus (says) Pilah-Eštar.
2. qi₂-bi-ma um-ma pi₂-la₂-ah-eš₁₈-dar-ma
3. a-hi a-ta be-li₂ a-ta
#tr.en.: You are my brother, you are my lord.
4. a-na-kam a-wa-tam₂ ša E₂.GAL-lim
5. mi₃-ma / i-še₂-me-ma
6. a-pu-tum i-na {d}UTU-ši
#tr.en.(o 10): Please, 
7. ṭup-pi₂ ta-ša-me-u₂
8. ša-ap₂-tam₂ ab₂-kam-ma
9. i-ti₂-iš-mu-ur-na
10. qa₂-i / a-na-kam
11. ši₂-ip-ru-u₂ a-na
@bottom
1. ka₃-ri-im ka₃-ni-iš₃
2. a-na a-li-ki-im
@reverse
1. ka₃-la₂-im e-ku-šu-nim
2. ši₂-ip-ru šu-[nu]
3. e ik-šu-du#-ni-ka₃-ma
4. e ta-se₂-ke-er#
$ end of side